@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@command{starter-web-ui} serves a browser dashboard. The C kernel owns
HTTP, MySQL execution, the http-bridge client, timers, and auth.
Guile registers widget types and always produces the refresh view-model
(@code{prepare} / @code{draw}). Live values come from
@command{starter-http-bridge}; charts query MySQL @code{labels}/@code{history}.

@node Building
@chapter Building

@example
./autogen.sh
./configure
make
./src/starter-web-ui -c examples/web-ui.xml
@end example

@node Configuration
@chapter Configuration

Two XML files:

@table @asis
@item Daemon config
Bind address/port, bridge URL, MySQL, auth, @code{data-dir}, paths.
@item User-config
Widget instances under @file{data-dir/user-config.xml}. Created empty;
rewritten atomically when the UI adds/edits/deletes widgets.
@end table

@node Architecture
@chapter Architecture

Refresh pipeline for every widget:

@enumerate
@item C timeout
@item hook @code{before-widget-refresh}
@item Guile @code{prepare} (SQL for history, or empty for live)
@item C fetch (MySQL or bridge)
@item Guile @code{draw} → JSON view-model
@item hook @code{after-widget-refresh}
@item Browser applies the view-model
@end enumerate

@node HTTP API
@chapter HTTP API

@table @code
@item GET /health
@item GET/POST /login, POST /logout
@item GET /session
@item GET /widget-types
@item GET /dashboard
@item POST /widgets, PUT/DELETE /widgets/@var{id}
@item GET /widgets/@var{id}/data
@item POST /widgets/@var{id}/action
@item GET /labels
@item /api/* 
Proxy to http-bridge
@end table

@node Guile widgets
@chapter Guile widgets

Use @code{(widget-type-register! #:type ... #:tags ... #:fields ...
#:prepare ... #:draw ...)} from @code{(web-ui core)}.
Built-ins: @code{toggle}, @code{slider}, @code{sensor}, @code{chart}.

Tags filter the editor wizard (@code{digital}/@code{analog},
@code{live}/@code{history}, @code{writable}, @dots{}).

@node Authentication
@chapter Authentication

Optional. @code{<auth method="none"/>} leaves the LAN open (admin-equivalent).
@code{method="password"} requires username/password; session cookie is
persistent (@code{HttpOnly}). Groups: @code{user} (view + live actions) and
@code{admin} (also edit dashboard).

@node Bridge writes and USR1
@chapter Bridge writes and USR1

Widget actions that change a live input always:

@enumerate
@item Read current flags from http-bridge
@item Set @code{val} and OR @code{USR1} (@code{0x1000000000000000})
@item Schedule a clear of @code{USR1} after @code{usr1-clear-timeout-sec}
      (daemon XML; @code{0} keeps the flag)
@end enumerate

All bridge @code{PUT}s use retries with bouncing backoff
(@code{bridge-put-retries}, @code{bridge-put-backoff-ms}).

